RE: The recent ideas for "magic-wand-created" traps:

What about bear traps?  Certainly you wouldn't create this with a wand, right?
If I wanted a bear trap, I would go to Asidonhopo's General Store and BUY
a bear trap (if I could find it, of course).  Then I'd apply it someplace and
step back!  If I was so careless as to stumble into a bear trap later on AND
I happened to have a lock pick, I could probably fiddle with the mechanism
and release it.  In fact, I could probably unlock the bear trap completely
(it's chained to the ground, you see...) so that I could take it with me
and set it someplace else.

Dart and arrow traps should be made out of darts and arrows (SURPRISE!)
(maybe a cross bow also).  Or, since these traps require a fair amount 
of skill (much more than setting a bear trap), maybe I shouldn't be able 
to set these at all.

Rust/gush-of-water traps are a classic:  the bucket of water balanced on
the half open door... Of course, these traps occur out in the middle of nowhere!
We'd also need buckets (or empty-potion bottles) and some way to fill them
up (fountains, of course).  What if you could prop any potion above a doorway?

	You see a door being opened. -More-
	The potion of paralysis spills onto the <insert monster> -More-
	The <monster> is frozen in it's tracks! -More-

	... and you run away while the door is blocked..
	(Yes a little contrived...)

Land-mines and exploding-door-KABOOM-traps:  either of these presupposes some
kind of explosive device.  How about a potion of nytroglicerine (sp)?  
This is something that can be made at home, and it's also pretty volatile.
Be careful running around the dungeon, and DON'T LET THE DRAGON BREATH FIRE
ON YOU----BOOOM!  

As for the truely magic traps (polymorph, magic/anti-magic, teleportation), 
these should be fairly difficult and expensive to create, more than just 
zapping a wand at the floor.  Just look at how much trouble other powerful-yet-
easy-to-use objects have caused:  polymorph wands, wish-wands, grenades, ...

At the very least, creating a magical trap with a wand should not only
use all charges of the wand, but also consume the wand itself (so you can't
just recharge it).  A small chance of failure would be appropriate
(not to injure the player--or not much :-)--but just to add some risk to
creating the trap.  Orrrr, maybe some type of "Permanency" spell should be
needed to make the trap stick.    Or even special objects, such as a 
cameleon corpse to make a polymorph trap, a dead quantum mechanic to make 
a teleport trap, a dead lich to make a magic trap....

Of course, there isn't much point in adding player created traps unless it
really adds something to the game, more than just something to fiddle with
when you're in Wizard mode.  Player-created traps should allow new ways
for clever, careful players to kill or evade monsters or defeat other traps or
puzzles in the dungeon.  For instance, something as simple as a bear trap 
could save your life if you set it in a doorway when being chased by a bunch
of nasties  (you may wonder how a little bear trap is going to stop a dragon,
but they always seem to stop *ME*, no matter how much super stength, armor,
etc, etc, I have).

One last frivolous thing:  how about adding a Pie Trap, a la 
	Gary Larson/Farside?    8-)

